# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# `app/page.tsx` is a server component whose entire body is
# `redirect("/dashboard")`. Under the standalone (Render) build the server
# issues a real 307. Under `output: "export"` there is no server, and the
# root page exports as `<html id="__next_error__">` — a Next.js error
# document. The build still exits 0 and prints `✓ Exporting (2/2)`, so
# nothing about the CI output would tell you the front door is broken.
#
# That was measured on the generated `out/index.html`, not assumed. It is
# the same class of defect this platform keeps hitting: a green build is
# not a working feature.
#
# Cloudflare Pages applies these rules before serving a file, so `/` is
# answered with a redirect and the error document is never reached.
#
# Harmless to the Render build: `public/` is copied verbatim into the
# image, where this is just an unused text file. Nothing needs undoing
# when the deployment moves back to Render.
/    /dashboard    302
